  "description": "captured-admission.v0 conformance vectors. The shared lifecycle CORE under review verdicts, contribution settlement, and TEE attestation epochs. Every verdict is recomputed by admission_check.py from the record alone. Two stored dimensions (lifecycle_state, disposition) live in separate namespaces; absence (liveness_failure) and conflict are DERIVED, never stored. Admission is a GATE: only an accepted admission creates an obligation (Pavlo). For an accepted obligation, SEMANTIC resolution and LIVENESS (deadline met/missed) are separate recomputable facts and are never collapsed -- a late disposition resolves without erasing the breach. Negative controls NC1-NC5 exercise the separations rather than assert them.",
  "profiles_note": "permitted_dispositions is the review-obligation completion set: verdict_published | cancelled (only if a real withdrawal path exists) | failed_with_reason. rejected_at_admission is NOT here -- it is an admission OUTCOME that creates no obligation. Settlement and TEE-epoch profiles supply their own vocabularies over the same core; a synchronous profile marks unreachable states (e.g. cancelled) unreachable-by-construction rather than building dead paths.",
